  "markdown": "Details\n\n# Seams, corners, edges and joins, up close\n\nA wallcovering is judged at the seam, in the corner and along the edge. These are our own photographs of those places, taken on finished and in-progress installations, each linked to the project it comes from.\n\n## Seams\n\nWhere one drop meets the next. On a tonal or plain ground there is no motif to hide a join, so each seam is butted and rolled until it disappears at normal viewing distance.\n\n![Seam detail in Cadence Oxblood.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/beverly-05-800.webp)\n\nA seam in Cadence Oxblood: a tonal ground, with no motif to hide the join. [Calico Wallpaper × BEVERLY 1975, The Lavery](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/calico-beverly-1975-cadence/)\n\n![Close detail of the entrance-hall wallcovering: soft horizontal bands of charcoal, silver and ochre, laid with no visible seam.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/fs-residences-03-800.webp)\n\nBanded entrance-hall wallcovering in charcoal, silver and ochre, laid with no visible seam. [Four Seasons Private Residences, Ten Trinity Square](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/four-seasons-ten-trinity-square/)\n\n## Internal corners\n\nA corner is where a pattern most often breaks. The paper is carried into the corner and the design is kept continuous across it, so the eye reads one wall, not two.\n\n![The mural wrapped around an internal corner, full height.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/heathrow-05-800.webp)\n\nA Calico Wallpaper landscape mural wrapped round an internal corner, full height. [Calico Wallpaper at Heathrow Terminal 4](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/heathrow-terminal-4-calico/)\n\n![Fromental silk wallcovering in a corner showing seamless pattern match, Four Seasons Hotel London at Ten Trinity Square.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/fs-ig-10-800.webp)\n\nFromental silk turning into a corner with the pattern matched across it. [Four Seasons Hotel London at Ten Trinity Square](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/four-seasons-ten-trinity-square/)\n\n## Edges\n\nExternal corners, arches and shadow gaps leave the cut edge on show. The line has to be straight, tight and even along its whole length; where a wall is not true, a bespoke trim makes the edge read as one line.\n\n![A wallcovered arch seen from below, its curved outer edge finished as one crisp, even line, framing a room with a decorative plaster ceiling and a chandelier.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/arch-trim-01-800.webp)\n\nA wallcovered arch, its curved outer edge finished as one crisp, even line. [A prime residence in central London](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/imperfect-arches-external-corner-trim/)\n\n![Close detail of a woven wallcovering on two neighbouring surfaces, each edge cut clean either side of a narrow shadow gap.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/arch-trim-09-800.webp)\n\nWoven wallcovering on two neighbouring surfaces, each edge cut clean either side of a narrow shadow gap. [A prime residence in central London](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/imperfect-arches-external-corner-trim/)\n\n![Close detail of a woven grasscloth wallcovering turning an external corner, the weave running straight and tight to the edge.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/fs-residences-06-800.webp)\n\nWoven grasscloth turning an external corner, the weave straight and tight to the edge. [Four Seasons Private Residences, Ten Trinity Square](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/four-seasons-ten-trinity-square/)\n\n## Joins\n\nWhere the wallcovering meets something else: a door frame, joinery, a skirting or a switch plate. The cut follows the fitting exactly, with no gap and no overlap.\n\n![Black matt Muraspec walls around a door with a brushed stainless-steel trim, Mercedes-AMG showroom, London.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/mercedes-amg-02-800.webp)\n\nBlack matt Muraspec walls meeting a brushed stainless-steel door trim. [Mercedes-AMG showroom, London](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/mercedes-amg-showroom-london/)\n\n![Fermoie linen applied to walls, joinery and skirting, a private project, London.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/brand-fermoie-01-800.webp)\n\nFermoie linen carried over the walls, joinery and skirting, photographed during the installation. [A private project, London](https://www.mrwallcover.com/materials/#maker-fermoie)\n\n![Close-up of a timber-grain wallcovering beside a light switch, Novotel London Canary Wharf.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/novotel-02-800.webp)\n\nTimber-grain wallcovering cut close round a light switch. [Novotel London Canary Wharf](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/novotel-london-canary-wharf/)\n\nThe method behind these finishes is in the [Wallcovering Guide](https://www.mrwallcover.com/advice/); for a room of your own, [send us the drawings or a photograph](https://www.mrwallcover.com/contact/?intent=install).\n\nBy [Dorin Burcus](https://www.mrwallcover.com/about/#dorin), founder\n",
